<p>As listed in <a href="#sensors-24-03458-t001" class="usa-link">Table 1</a>, systems that can be affected by a cyberattack include navigational and surveillance systems, such as ECDIS and GNSS. Further investigations confirmed the systems under attack as depicted in <a href="#sensors-24-03458-t001" class="usa-link">Table 1</a> and provided more insights as to the vulnerable systems that exist on ships and onshore maritime infrastructures/centers [<a href="#B2-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B2-sensors-24-03458">2</a>,<a href="#B7-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B7-sensors-24-03458">7</a>,<a href="#B8-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B8-sensors-24-03458">8</a>,<a href="#B25-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B25-sensors-24-03458">25</a>,<a href="#B34-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B34-sensors-24-03458">34</a>,<a href="#B35-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B35-sensors-24-03458">35</a>,<a href="#B36-sensors-24-03458" class="usa-link" aria-describedby="B36-sensors-24-03458">36</a>]. As <a href="#sensors-24-03458-f004" class="usa-link">Figure 4</a> highlights, vulnerable systems include sensors, communication or management/control systems.</p>
